From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:07:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: document the failed timestamp-UNBIND state

A failed drain leaves the handle unpublished and the mapping retained
until file teardown; a retry returns ENOENT. Noted in review.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_drm.rs | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_drm.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_drm.rs
index 5b206acff1e7..6c849102bdad 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_drm.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_drm.rs
@@ -1074,8 +1074,9 @@ fn bind_object(
                 let timestamp = state.timestamps.swap_remove(index);
                 // Only this file's submissions can reference the binding. Wait
                 // for each of its VMs' own work (progress-based), not for
-                // every client's. On failure the mapping stays retained, and
-                // file teardown handles it as before.
+                // every client's. On failure the handle is already gone: the
+                // mapping stays retained until file teardown, and a retry of
+                // this UNBIND returns ENOENT.
                 let mut ids = KVec::new();
                 for vm in state.vms.iter() {
                     ids.push(vm.id, GFP_KERNEL)?;
